Practical 4 – Implement SPAN
Topology: Devices used: - 1 Switch (2960-24TT)- 1 PC - connected to Switch- 1 Server - connected to Switch - 1 Sniffer - connected to Switch

4. IP Configuration
Device	 IP Address	 Subnet Mask
PC0	   | 10.1.1.100 |	255.255.255.0
Server0| 10.1.1.200	| 255.255.255.0

5. Switch Configuration
Open the switch CLI and enter:
enable
configure terminal
monitor session 1 source interface fa0/1
monitor session 1 destination interface fa0/3
end


6. Configure the Sniffer
1. Click Sniffer0.
2. Open the GUI tab.
3. Set Service → On.
4. Under Incoming Packets, select Port0 (the journal screenshot shows Port0).
5. Click Clear to clear the existing filters.
6. Select only ICMP from the filter list.


7. Verification
On PC0:
1. Open Desktop → Command Prompt.
2. Ping the server:
ping 10.1.1.200


3. Open Sniffer0 GUI and check the captured packets. You should see ICMP traffic.

On the switch, you can also verify SPAN:
show monitor
